    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27343" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyciscus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυκίσκος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a wolfdog</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lycisci dicuntur canes nati ex lupis et
					canibus, cum inter se forte miscentur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 12, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyciscus</span></b> , <i>the name of a beautiful boy</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. Epod.
				11, 24</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A boy whose statue was made by Leochares</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 8,
				19, § 79</span></i>.</div>
